# AGENTS.md — Royo Farm Manager · Android rebuild playbook

This file is the single source of truth for an AI agent (or developer) asked to **reproduce the Royo Farm Manager app from scratch as a native Android Studio project in Kotlin, using Firebase**. It contains the full data model, security rules, business logic, screen-by-screen UI spec, project scaffold and an ordered build plan. Nothing else about the original web app is needed.

> Target: a working, installable Android app with feature parity. No backend of your own — Firebase Auth + Cloud Firestore only.

---

## 0. Ground rules for the agent

1. **Create a real Android Studio project** (Gradle KTS, Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3). Not a web app, not Compose Multiplatform, not Flutter.
2. **Follow this document literally.** Everything the product needs is specified here. Do not add features, screens, payments, ads, AI chat or extra charts.
3. **Parity means parity**, including the gaps listed in §12 — the original app has create + read only (no edit/delete UI), and its stock/production side effects are two separate writes.
4. Build in the order of §11 and run the acceptance checklist (§13) before declaring done.
5. UI text is **English**, currency **UGX**, dates **en-GB**, all date maths **UTC**.
6. If a Firebase project/`google-services.json` is unavailable, still generate all code and Gradle config, leave a clearly labelled placeholder file and a `README_LOCAL_SETUP.md` explaining where to drop the real one.

